+ * DMA2D-friendly vertical gradient. A vertical gradient quantized to RGB565
+ * collapses into a small number of solid horizontal bands (e.g. 12 for the lock
+ * screen's dark-blue -> black over 340 px). This draws each band as a solid,
+ * radius-0 rect via LV_EVENT_DRAW_MAIN, so every band routes through the DMA2D
+ * register-to-memory fill instead of a per-pixel SW gradient. Visually identical
+ * to cellphone_obj_paint_grad on an RGB565 display (no dithering). Best for dark
+ * gradients with few bands; bright gradients (white->black, ~32 bands) gain less.
+ */
+void cellphone_obj_paint_grad_banded(lv_obj_t * obj, lv_color_t top, lv_color_t bot);
